use `nix-shell -p nodejs --run \"...\"` for npm/npx commands\n- `npm install` needed before tests (no node_modules checked in)\n\n## Architecture\n- `assets/renderer.ts` - Framework renderer interface (`FrameworkRenderer`)\n- `assets/renderers/vue.ts` - Vue implementation of FrameworkRenderer\n- `assets/hooks.ts` - `getRendererHook()` (framework-agnostic) + `getVueHook()` (legacy Vue-specific)\n- `assets/server.ts` - `getRendererRender()` (framework-agnostic SSR) + `getRender()` (legacy Vue SSR)\n- All existing Vue APIs preserved for backward compatibility\n\n## Key Patterns\n- Hook stores renderer state as `this.vue` (even for non-Vue renderers, for backward compat)\n- Slots flow as raw HTML strings to the renderer; renderer converts to framework-specific format\n- Props parsed from DOM attributes are plain objects; renderer wraps in its reactivity system\n- JSON Patch library (`jsonPatch.ts`) is framework-agnostic, operates on plain objects\n","numLines":19,"startLine":1,"totalLines":19}}}
