{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01T4cB96TN3ux75yscf7vehP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's a summary of what was done for US-004:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. Elixir: `lib/live_vite.ex`\n- Added `data-framework=\"vue\"` attribute to the component `<div>` template, so the client-side hook can identify which framework renderer to use.\n\n### 2. TypeScript: `assets/hooks.ts`\n- **New `RendererEntry` interface** — pairs a `FrameworkRenderer` with its `resolve` function.\n- **New `getMultiRendererHook(renderers)`** — the core new function. Creates a single LiveView hook that:\n  - Reads `data-framework` from the DOM element on mount\n  - Dispatches to the correct renderer from a `Record<string, RendererEntry>` registry\n  - Falls back to the sole renderer when only one is registered (backward compat)\n  - Stores the active renderer on `this.__renderer` for use in `updated`/`destroyed`\n  - Throws descriptive errors for unknown or missing framework attributes\n- **Refactored `getRendererHook(renderer, resolve)`** — now delegates to `getMultiRendererHook` with a single entry, keeping the existing API intact.\n- All shared hook logic (JSON patch, slot parsing, handler parsing, prop diffing) stays in the hook layer — only framework-specific operations are delegated.\n\n### 3. TypeScript: `assets/index.ts`\n- Exported `getMultiRendererHook` and `RendererEntry` type.\n\n### 4. Tests: `assets/renderer.test.ts`\n- Added `getMultiRendererHook` test suite covering:\n  - Multi-renderer dispatch (vue vs react based on `data-framework`)\n  - Error on unknown framework\n  - Error on missing `data-framework` with multiple renderers\n  - Correct renderer used across `mounted`/`updated`/`destroyed` lifecycle\n  - Single-renderer fallback when `data-framework` is absent\n\n### Test Results\n- **253/253 Vitest tests pass** (including 21 renderer tests with new multi-renderer coverage)\n- **172/178 Elixir tests p